# Build-specific ignore for docker/Dockerfile.audit. BuildKit uses this in
# preference to the repo-root .dockerignore when building this Dockerfile.
#
# Why it differs from the root .dockerignore: the root one excludes all of
# proofs/, but build.rs (ceremony check #1) and the lib's `include_str!` need
# the committed ZK vkeys + manifests at BUILD time. We keep ONLY those small
# text files and still drop the multi-hundred-MB .ptau and the gitignored
# runtime artifacts (.wasm/.r1cs/.ark.zkey — those are mounted at runtime).
#
# Patterns are relative to the build context root (the repo root). The
# single-level `dir/*` + `!dir/sub` idiom is deliberate: a `proofs/**` exclude
# would make the deep `!proofs/keys/...` re-includes impossible (Docker cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory was excluded).

.git
target
**/target
node_modules
**/node_modules
.claude
app/public-ui/dist
*.log

# Keep only proofs/keys/{verification_keys,manifests}; drop everything else
# under proofs/ (circuits, build/, setup scripts, and especially the .ptau).
proofs/*
!proofs/keys
proofs/keys/*
!proofs/keys/verification_keys
!proofs/keys/manifests

# ...and proofs/zkvm/canonicalization/, which the lib pulls in at COMPILE time:
# zk/canonicalization.rs `include_bytes!`s the RISC Zero guest ELF and
# `include_str!`s its image ID (the fixed-image receipt verified as part of the
# public unified_canonicalization_inclusion_root protocol), and a test reads
# receipt-fixture.json. Dropping these fails the build with
# "couldn't read .../olympus_canonicalization_guest.elf". The whole directory is
# ~1.3 MB — it carries no large proving artifact, so keep it wholesale rather
# than enumerating three files that the code may add to.
!proofs/zkvm
proofs/zkvm/*
!proofs/zkvm/canonicalization
